---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { attributions } from '../lib/internships.js';
const path = '/disclaimer/';
---
<Base
  title="Disclaimer and data sources | Universities500"
  description="Where Universities500 gets its facts, how courses, scholarships, internships and MBA programmes are read, and what to check before you act."
  path={path}
>
  <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span>Disclaimer and data sources</nav>
  <h1>Disclaimer and data sources</h1>
  <p class="lead">One page for how this site works, so the other pages can stay short. Every page still shows where its facts came from and the date they were read.</p>

  <section aria-labelledby="d-use">
    <h2 id="d-use">Use this site to get started</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Fees, deadlines, entry rules and visa rules change often and can differ by intake and by country of citizenship. Check the official page before you apply, pay or book.</li>
      <li>Nothing here is legal, immigration, financial or admissions advice. We do not represent any university, lender, test provider or government.</li>
      <li>A fact the official page did not state is shown as "Not stated" or "Check the official page". We do not estimate it and we do not take it from third-party sites.</li>
      <li>We show no rankings, we publish none of our own, and no ranking is used to order a list. The <a href="/rankings/">rankings page</a> links to the ranking sites so you can check them yourself.</li>
      <li>Found a mistake? Check the university's own page, which is the source of truth, and let us know.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="d-courses">
    <h2 id="d-courses">Courses</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A program reads course pages on each university's own website. It follows each site's robots.txt, reads slowly and never goes around a block. <a href="/bot/">About our reader</a>.</li>
      <li>A course is kept only if its page shows a Bachelor's or Master's, full-time study on campus, and that it is open to international students. Online, part-time, foundation, diploma and research degrees are left out.</li>
      <li>Every figure on a course page was copied from that page. Where the page did not state a fact, the course page says so.</li>
      <li>The field is our own label, chosen from words in the course name. It is not the university's.</li>
      <li>Not every course of every university is here yet. Some websites cannot be read by a program.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="d-mba">
    <h2 id="d-mba">MBA Explorer</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Each programme's facts come from the school's own pages, and each fact shows the sentence it was copied from.</li>
      <li>The tracks follow the minimum work experience the school's page states. A master's in management or a deferred MBA is for recent graduates and is labelled so.</li>
      <li>For careers we link to each school's own employment report instead of re-publishing its numbers.</li>
      <li>The first set was read by hand from the school pages. A program that uses no AI takes over from there, and each record shows the date it was last read.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="d-sch">
    <h2 id="d-sch">Scholarships</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A program reads public scholarship pages from official programme sites and from each university's own website every two days.</li>
      <li>Only scholarships open to international students on Bachelor's or Master's courses are kept.</li>
      <li>Open, closed or yet to open comes only from dates on the official page. With no dates, the status is "Check the official page".</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="d-int">
    <h2 id="d-int">Internships</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A program reads the public job feeds that employers publish through their careers pages, and two open job feeds, once a day.</li>
      <li>A listing is kept only if its title names an internship, co-op, placement or working-student role, and its location is clearly in one of our destinations.</li>
      <li>We copy the title, company, city and link. The description and the application stay on the employer's page. A listing disappears when the employer takes it down.</li>
      <li>Whether you may work on your visa depends on your visa and your course. We do not say who is eligible for a listing.</li>
      {attributions.map((a) => <li>{a}</li>)}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="d-uni">
    <h2 id="d-uni">Universities</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Overview text on a university page is from <a href="https://www.wikipedia.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikipedia</a>, licensed <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>. Each university page links to its article and says when the text was shortened.</li>
      <li>Founding year, campuses, student numbers and people who studied there come from <a href="https://www.wikidata.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikidata</a> (CC0). It is open data and can be out of date.</li>
      <li>The website and social accounts are the ones the university lists on Wikidata.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="d-news">
    <h2 id="d-news">Industry news</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Short excerpts of official notices from government and immigration bodies and official study agencies, checked every day, each linked to the official page. Trade-press items show a headline, a date and a link only.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>
